{
  "about": "The meld: at rest the L and the o are one rounded triangle. As the o leaves it takes its mass with it: the corner drains like a pool, a liquid neck stretches and snaps, and the ball overshoots and settles in the socket. Times are in seconds and match the preview SVGs in this folder. Each key's ease applies to the segment that ends at that key.",
  "coordinates": {
    "units": "The same units as logo/mark.svg, whose viewBox is 12 12 76 76. Mark previews use viewBox 0 0 100 100; lockup previews use 0 0 193 100, the same placement as logo/lockup.svg plus a 12-unit margin.",
    "axis": "h is distance from the socket centre along the outward diagonal (1, -1)/sqrt(2). A ball at h sits at (56 + h/sqrt(2), 44 - h/sqrt(2))."
  },
  "geometry": {
    "lShape": "M12 21A9 9 0 0 1 30 21V44A26 26 0 0 0 56 70H79A9 9 0 0 1 79 88H20Q12 88 12 80Z",
    "socketCentre": [
      56,
      44
    ],
    "socketRadius": 26,
    "ballAtRest": {
      "h": 12.7279,
      "centre": [
        65,
        35
      ],
      "radius": 21
    },
    "triangleFill": "The fill that turns the L into a rounded triangle: points with x >= 27.4, y <= 72.6 and x - y <= 12.728, and, where x < 56 and y > 44, within 28.6 of the socket centre. Its edges tuck under the L. Its area roughly equals the ball's, so mass looks conserved.",
    "pool": "The triangle fill clipped to h <= level. \"full\" is the hypotenuse (h = 0.515); \"empty\" is the socket wall (h = -26) or below.",
    "ball": "An ellipse at (x, y) with radii rx, ry, rotated by angle degrees (rx lies along the angle). The default -45 points rx outward along the axis.",
    "neck": "Two thin concave cones on the axis, drawn only into the goo layer, never as crisp shapes. Back cone: base 3 units inside the ball's back edge with the given half-width, tip backLength behind that edge. Pool cone: base 3 units inside the pool surface, tip poolLength in front of it. Each side is a quadratic curve whose control point sits halfway along at 0.45 of the half-width. null means no neck."
  },
  "goo": {
    "how": "Blur the pool, balls and neck together, then threshold the alpha so overlapping blurs fuse into one liquid outline. Draw crisp copies of the L, pool and balls on top so edges stay sharp; the neck shows only where it fuses.",
    "blurSigma": 4.2,
    "alphaThreshold": "alpha' = clamp(48 * alpha - 26), an edge at about 0.54",
    "native": "In SwiftUI, a Canvas with a blur filter followed by an alpha threshold filter (GraphicsContext.Filter.alphaThreshold) gives the same effect; a small Metal shader also works."
  },
  "easing": {
    "linear": [
      0,
      0,
      1,
      1
    ],
    "inOut": [
      0.45,
      0,
      0.55,
      1
    ],
    "in": [
      0.6,
      0,
      0.9,
      0.5
    ],
    "out": [
      0.2,
      0.7,
      0.3,
      1
    ]
  },
  "rules": [
    "One color, the same as the static mark. The accent never appears in motion either.",
    "Each animation plays once and ends on the static mark or lockup, except the meld loop, which repeats while something loads.",
    "The fades at the start and end of the preview files exist only so the previews loop. Leave them out in the app.",
    "When Reduce Motion is on, show the static mark or lockup and skip the animation."
  ],
